      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T14:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nice catch on the behavior difference. I updated Plot and RasterMaskHelper to support initialization of the padding to a caller-provided value. \n\nI know we need to (sometimes) clear the mask bounds to something other than zero but do we ever access sample the padding for clips? I wasn\u0027t sure why we used padding for clip masks. I had assumed they were always nearest sampled, but I didn\u0027t investigate that.\n\nAlso, I was curious about inverse fill for path-atlas when allowing bilinear interpolation (android). I guess we invert in the shader, so clearing to zero is always ok?",
      "parentUuid": "5c044d1b_2b4f782b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "4357b0495547f4653f3de1ada1abc2001af0aafd",
